From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:11:21 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: add the LDP and STP instructions

LDP and STP, in the signed offset form, are available as intrinsics in
the W and X forms. The two registers go through a single memory argument
of twice their size, so the semantics only splits or packs that value.
A memory-argument condition restricts the address to a base register and
a scaled 7-bit offset.

LDP is also a load for lower_glob_load, so it can read global arrays.
The printer refuses an LDP whose two destinations are the same register,
which register allocation does not produce.

Co-authored-by: orvenweb3 <orvenweb3@gmail.com>
